# KNOWN GAP — the f-string interpolation error-retention WHITELIST still
# swallows most semantic errors. `E_NotIndexable` was added to it by XXIX-A's
# residual fix (`8867be1a`); the arms around it are still dropped.
#
# This file is the UNDEFINED-NAME cell, which is the most user-visible: a
# typo'd identifier inside an f-string is silently accepted AND LOWERED TO 0.
#
# MEASURED AT HEAD (2026-08-04), post-`8867be1a`:
#   int x = nope              -> error[E_UndefinedName]      (rejects)
#   print(f"{nope}")          -> "OK: no semantic errors"    <-- THIS FILE
#                                builds, runs, prints `0`
#
# CONFIRMED SIBLING CELLS (same mechanism, same one-line-per-arm fix):
#   helper(1) with arity 2    outside -> error[E_WrongArgCount]
#                             inside  -> "OK: no semantic errors"
#   no_such_fn(1)             inside  -> "OK: no semantic errors"
# ⚠ This is a SAMPLE, not a total enumeration: the whitelist RETAINS 5 arms
# (NoMethodFound, MethodGenericInferenceFailed, UnwrapOnNonOptional,
# NotIndexable, NotIndexableMut) and DROPS everything else, so every other
# typecheck error kind is a candidate cell. Whoever fixes this should enumerate
# from the error enum, not from this list.
#
# NOT swallowed (different pass, correctly rejects inside f-strings):
#   E_UseAfterMove  — the safety pass, not the typecheck interp path
#   E_NoMethodFound — on the retention whitelist
#
# ROOT: `src/semantic/typecheck.rs` `Expr::StringLiteral` arm (~:1313)
# typechecks each interpolation segment, then FILTERS the emitted errors
# through the retain-whitelist. Anything not listed is discarded silently, so
# the DEFAULT for a newly-added check is "invisible inside f-strings".
#
# ATTRIBUTION: pre-existing debt (the whitelist predates Round XXIX — it comes
# from the round-31 primitive-method reject), SURFACED by XXIX-A's residual fix
# which had to add two arms to it. Not owed by XXIX-A; it is one line per arm
# in the site that fix already touched, and the new
# `tests/lints.rs::interp_error_retention_arms_count` pin makes any change to
# the list a reviewed action rather than a silent one.
#
# ⚠ This mechanism is ALSO why AGENTS.md Core #15(d) says never probe
# accept/reject inside an f-string. The documented probe hazard and this
# compiler defect are the same thing — which is why it reads as a testing
# artifact and survived.
#
# INTENDED: `error[E_UndefinedName]` here, exactly as outside the f-string.
int main():
    print(f"{nope}")
    return 0
